method.description:
Returns the shared GPU data buffer to bind in your own uniform set, or an invalid [RID] if [method _get_gpu_data_size] returns 0.
All environments share this one buffer, so your compute shader must index it by [method get_env_index]. Pass that index in your own push constant — writing to the wrong slice silently corrupts another environment's data.
[codeblock]
var data := RDUniform.new()
data.uniform_type = RenderingDevice.UNIFORM_TYPE_STORAGE_BUFFER
data.binding = 2
data.add_id(agent.get_gpu_buffer_rid())
_uniform_set = rd.uniform_set_create([data], shader, 0)

# Then, per dispatch — the index must reach the shader somehow:
var push_constants := PackedByteArray()
push_constants.resize(16)
push_constants.encode_u32(0, agent.get_env_index())
[/codeblock]
And in the compute shader:
[codeblock]
layout(set = 0, binding = 2, std430) buffer VGAData {
    uint collected[];
};
layout(push_constant, std430) uniform PushConstants {
    uint env_index;
} pc;

void main() {
    // ...
    atomicAdd(collected[pc.env_index], 1u);
}
[/codeblock]
